.TH NJORD 1 "October 2026" "Njord 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
njord \- Skadi's optional compressed IMAP proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B njord --upstream
.I hostname
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Njord forwards bytes between each client and a separate provider connection.
Skadi connections use checksummed zstd level 22 frames in both directions.
Providers use conventional IMAP. Explicit HTTPS image requests receive smaller
WebP previews, or original bytes on request. Automatic IMAP replay is not implemented.
Njord is native C++ using libevent, OpenSSL, zstd, libcurl and WebP.
.PP
By default Njord listens on 127.0.0.1:1143 and connects to the provider
using verified TLS on port 993. Provider credentials pass through the relay;
they are never logged. Use listener TLS or an encrypted tunnel for remote access.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --upstream " HOST"
Required provider hostname; also used for TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.BI --upstream-port " PORT"
Provider port. Defaults to 993, or 143 with --upstream-plaintext.
.TP
.B --upstream-plaintext
Forward raw TCP instead of establishing upstream TLS. Njord does not negotiate
STARTTLS. With --raw, a tunnel can pass an end-to-end TLS conversation.
.TP
.BI --upstream-ca " FILE"
CA certificate file for upstream verification. Verification is never disabled.
.TP
.BI --listen " ADDRESS"
Numeric listen address; defaults to 127.0.0.1. IPv4 and IPv6 are supported.
.TP
.BI --port " PORT"
Listen port; defaults to 1143. Zero requests an available port from the OS.
.TP
.BI --certfile " FILE"
Enable implicit listener TLS using this certificate chain.
.TP
.BI --keyfile " FILE"
Listener private key. Must be specified together with --certfile.
.TP
.BI --connect-timeout " SECONDS"
DNS, connection, and TLS handshake timeout. Listener TLS and upstream setup
each get a deadline. Defaults to 30 seconds.
Established sessions have no application idle timeout.
.TP
.BI --shutdown-timeout " SECONDS"
Graceful drain and TLS shutdown deadline; defaults to 30 seconds. On expiry,
remaining connections are aborted and the event is logged.
.TP
.B --raw
Use an ordinary uncompressed TCP relay for clients without the Njord protocol.
.TP
.BI --image-width " PIXELS"
Longest preview dimension; default 1024. WebP permits 1 through 16383.
.TP
.BI --image-quality " NUMBER"
WebP preview quality, 0 through 100; default 65.
.TP
.BI --image-timeout " SECONDS"
Deadline for each HTTPS image transfer; default 60.
.TP
.BI --image-ca " FILE"
CA bundle for HTTPS images. The default is system trust.
.TP
.B --image-allow-private
Allow image fetches to private network addresses, rejected by default.
.TP
.B --verbose
Log connection diagnostics, never mail contents or credentials.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage and exit.
.SH OPERATION
Traffic is streamed with backpressure and no application message-size limit.
Plain TCP half-closes are forwarded. TLS EOF ends the session because TLS
does not support independent write-half shutdown.
SIGINT and SIGTERM stop the listener and disconnect all sessions.
.SH SKADI
Use {localhost:1143/njord}INBOX for a local or tunneled listener, or
{home.example.com:1993/njord/ssl}INBOX for an implicit TLS listener.
Without /njord, Skadi uses normal IMAP.
.PP
K (sYnc) batches uncached headers and downloads selected message bodies.
[ (PartSizes) inspects attachment metadata without fetching contents.
Activate HTTPS image handles to fetch previews; O requests the original.
.PP
Restrict listener access to trusted clients. The image endpoint does not
require an IMAP login; use firewall rules, a VPN or SSH forwarding.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
njord --upstream imap.example.com
.fi
